The attached image displays flow cytometry histograms showing the effect of Nano-11 on costimulatory molecule expression by dendritic cells. Comparing Nano-11-treated cells (black line) to a medium control (gray line), there is a modest increase in CD40 expression and a significant upregulation of CD80 and CD86 on dendritic cells after two days of incubation. This indicates that Nano-11 activates dendritic cells, enhancing their ability to present antigens and stimulating an immune response, a key finding in the context of its evaluation as a vaccine adjuvant.